# EXAMNIA Phase 5 - completed reviews and stored-grade reporting.
# VS Code REST Client variables; copy requests into Postman if preferred.
# Configure MySQL and apply the existing migrations from Backend/ before use.
# php artisan db:seed supplies the demo accounts below, but no completed attempts.
# Use phase-4-api.http to start, answer, and finish an attempt for review examples.
# Replace all PASTE_* values with IDs/tokens returned by your local API or class context.
# Existing authentication, authoring, and attempt examples remain in phase-1/3/4-api.http.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000/api
@studentToken = PASTE_STUDENT_LOGIN_DATA_TOKEN
@teacherToken = PASTE_TEACHER_LOGIN_DATA_TOKEN
@classId = PASTE_CLASS_ID
@quizId = PASTE_QUIZ_ID_IN_THAT_CLASS
@attemptId = PASTE_FINISHED_ATTEMPT_ID
@studentId = PASTE_STUDENT_ID_FROM_GRADEBOOK_OR_ATTEMPT

### Student login - 200. Copy data.token into studentToken.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student1@example.test",
  "password": "DemoPassword123!",
  "device_name": "phase-five-student"
}

### Teacher login - 200. Copy data.token into teacherToken.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "teacher@example.test",
  "password": "DemoPassword123!",
  "device_name": "phase-five-teacher"
}

### Personal grade summary and attempt history - 200; authenticated student only.
# data.items contains individual attempts, including retakes, with stored metadata/grades.
# data.summary covers ALL matching attempts, not only the current page.
# No question text, selected answers, or option keys are included in these list rows.
GET {{baseUrl}}/students/me/grades?page=1&per_page=20
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Filter personal history by class, quiz, and status - 200.
# Supported status values: ongoing|finished. All ID filters are positive integers.
# Filters only narrow this student's own history; a student_id query cannot select another user.
# An unrelated/nonexistent class or quiz filter produces an empty own-history result.
GET {{baseUrl}}/students/me/grades?class_id={{classId}}&quiz_id={{quizId}}&status=finished&page=1&per_page=20
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Review the student's own finished attempt - 200.
# data.attempt contains stored result metadata; data.quiz/student identify the record.
# data.questions includes every question and options with is_correct for authorized review.
# question.answer is the saved choice/correctness/time, or null for an unanswered question.
# An ongoing attempt or another student's attempt returns 403 before answer keys are exposed.
GET {{baseUrl}}/attempts/{{attemptId}}/review
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Teacher class gradebook - 200; only classes owned by this teacher.
# data.items is a paginated STUDENT list, not a list of attempts.
# Each row has student identity, enrollment_status (enrolled|former), and its summary.
# Current students without attempts remain visible with zero counts and null grade statistics.
# Former members with attempt history in this class remain visible as historical rows.
# data.summary covers all class attempts, independently of student-row pagination.
GET {{baseUrl}}/classes/{{classId}}/gradebook?page=1&per_page=20
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}

### Limit a class gradebook to one quiz in that class - 200.
# quizId must belong to classId; a quiz outside the selected class returns 404.
# data.quiz identifies the selected quiz. Current class members remain visible with zero
# counts when they have no attempt for the selected quiz.
GET {{baseUrl}}/classes/{{classId}}/gradebook?quiz_id={{quizId}}&page=1&per_page=20
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}

### Teacher per-quiz grades - 200; quiz's class must belong to the teacher.
# data.items contains individual attempts with student identities and stored result metadata.
# data.summary covers all matching quiz attempts, including rows beyond this page.
# Ongoing rows have final_grade:null and graded:false; list rows never contain answer keys.
GET {{baseUrl}}/quizzes/{{quizId}}/grades?page=1&per_page=20
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}

### Filter one quiz's attempts by student and status - 200.
# Copy studentId from an authorized gradebook row or attempt response.
# Filters stay inside quizId's already authorized scope.
GET {{baseUrl}}/quizzes/{{quizId}}/grades?student_id={{studentId}}&status=finished&page=1&per_page=20
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}

### Teacher per-student answer detail through a finished attempt review - 200.
# quizId must be the attempt's actual quiz. A mismatched URL parent returns 404.
# The teacher must own that quiz's class, and the attempt must be finished.
# The response includes the student's saved answers and the question/option answer keys.
GET {{baseUrl}}/quizzes/{{quizId}}/attempts/{{attemptId}}/review
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}

# All five reporting endpoints return 200 on success using the existing envelope:
# {"success":true,"message":"...","data":...}
#
# List responses include data.pagination:
# {"current_page":1,"last_page":1,"per_page":20,"total":0}
# page must be an integer >=1; per_page must be an integer from 1 through 100.
#
# Summary keys:
# attempts_count, ongoing_count, finished_count, graded_count, ungraded_finished_count,
# average_grade, highest_grade, lowest_grade.
# Counts are integers; grade statistics are two-decimal strings or null.
# Only FINISHED attempts with a non-null stored final_grade enter grade statistics.
# A real grade of 0.00 is included; legacy missing grades stay null and are counted as
# ungraded finished attempts. An empty report has null grade statistics, not a fabricated zero.
# Retakes remain separate rows; averages describe the included attempts without selecting
# an official best/latest attempt or changing the stored final grade.
#
# Report reads use saved grades and do not regrade from current scoring configuration.
# No grade-list/gradebook response exposes questions, answers, or option correctness keys.
# Only an authorized FINISHED-attempt review returns option is_correct values.
# Legacy report rows do not require a scoring-rules snapshot merely to show stored data.
#
# Error envelope:
# {"success":false,"message":"...","error":{"code":"...","details":{}}}
# 401: missing, invalid, expired, or revoked token.
# 403: wrong role, another student's review, another teacher's class/quiz, or unfinished review.
# 404: missing resource, or an attempt/quiz not under the URL's selected parent.
# 422: invalid pagination, status, or positive-integer ID filter.
# Students and administrators do not receive an implicit teacher reporting bypass.
